## 3. DOCUMENT CHECKLIST\
\
### REQUIRED FOR AUBURN CITY PERMIT:\
\
**Application Documents:**\
- [ ] Completed Sign Permit Application (obtain from City Hall)\
- [ ] Cover Letter (draft included above \'96 print and sign)\
- [ ] Application Fee ($____ \'96 call 260-925-1234 to confirm amount)\
\
**Property Documentation:**\
- [ ] Proof of property ownership OR\
- [ ] Lease agreement showing right to install sign OR\
- [ ] Landlord consent letter (if tenant)\
- [ ] Site plan showing property lines and sign location\
\
**Sign Documentation:**\
- [ ] Photos of damaged sign (multiple angles)\
- [ ] Photos of sign location (showing surrounding area)\
- [ ] Drawing/sketch of proposed sign with dimensions\
- [ ] Elevation drawing showing height from grade\
- [ ] Electrical plans (if illuminated)\
\
**Storm Damage Documentation:**\
- [ ] Photos clearly showing storm damage\
- [ ] Date of damage\
- [ ] Insurance claim documentation (if filed)\
- [ ] Weather report/news article confirming storm (optional but helpful)\
\
**Contractor Documentation:**\
- [ ] Sign contractor name and contact\
- [ ] Contractor license (if required)\
- [ ] Electrical contractor info (if illuminated)\
\
### POTENTIALLY REQUIRED \'96 INDOT (State Highway):\
\
Since your property fronts IN-8 (Indiana State Road 8), you may need an **INDOT encroachment permit** if the sign is within the state right-of-way.\
\
**Contact:**\
- **INDOT Fort Wayne District** \'96 (260) 461-3301\
- **Ask for:** Permits Office\
\
**Typical INDOT Requirements:**\
- [ ] INDOT Encroachment Permit Application\
- [ ] Site plan showing distance from highway centerline\
- [ ] Proof sign is outside clear zone OR engineering justification\
- [ ] $100-200 permit fee\
\
**Right-of-Way Note:** INDOT typically controls 30-50 feet from centerline of state highways. If your sign is within this area, you need their permit IN ADDITION TO the city permit.\
