## 5. NEXT STEPS\
\
1. **Call Auburn City Hall (260-925-1234)**\
   - Confirm which department handles sign permits\
   - Ask for the official application form\
   - Confirm permit fee amount\
   - Ask about expedited processing for storm damage\
\
2. **Measure Your Existing Sign** (if still partially standing)\
   - Height, width, area\
   - Distance from property lines\
   - Distance from IN-8\
\
3. **Take Photos**\
   - Damaged sign (multiple angles)\
   - Sign location/area\
   - Wide shot showing property context\
\
4. **Check INDOT Requirements**\
   - Call Fort Wayne District: 260-461-3301\
   - Ask if sign is in state right-of-way\
   - Request encroachment permit if needed\
\
5. **Get Contractor Quotes**\
   - Sign company for replacement\
   - Electrician if illuminated\
   - Ask contractors if they handle permits (some do)\
\
6. **Submit Applications**\
   - City permit first (usually)\
   - INDOT permit simultaneously if required\
\
7. **Schedule Inspection**\
   - City will inspect after installation\
   - INDOT may inspect if state permit required\
\
---\
\
## 6. INSURANCE CLAIM NOTES\
\
**If filing an insurance claim:**\
\
1. **Document everything before removal**\
   - Photos of damaged sign\
   - Photos of surrounding area\
   - Keep damaged sign pieces if possible\
\
2. **Get replacement estimate**\
   - Sign company quote\
   - Permit fees\
   - Installation costs\
   - Electrical work (if applicable)\
\
3. **Policy check:**\
   - Is your coverage "replacement cost" or "actual cash value"?\
   - Replacement cost = full replacement amount\
   - Actual cash value = replacement minus depreciation\
\
4. **Business interruption:**\
   - Some policies cover lost revenue from damaged signage\
   - Ask your adjuster about this coverage\
